00\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�A\u0000\u0000customXml/itemProps1.xmlPK\u0001\u0002-\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u0000�$\u0007\u000f�\u0014\u0000\u0000��\u0001\u0000\u0012\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0014C\u0000\u0000word/numbering.xmlPK\u0001\u0002-\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u0000�v�G�\u000e\u0000\u0000l�\u0000\u0000\u000f\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�W\u0000\u0000word/styles.xmlPK\u0001\u0002-\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u0000�k\u0013�\u0001\u0002\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�f\u0000\u0000word/webSettings.xmlPK\u0001\u0002-\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u0000��`�\u0002\u0000\u0000�\u000b\u0000\u0000\u0012\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�h\u0000\u0000word/fontTable.xmlPK\u0001\u0002-\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u0000���6�\u0001\u0000\u0000�\u0002\u0000\u0000\u0011\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�k\u0000\u0000docProps/core.xmlPK\u0001\u0002-\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u0000��/\u0011\u0002\u0000\u0000\u001a\u0004\u0000\u0000\u0010\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�n\u0000\u0000docProps/app.xmlPK\u0001\u0002-\u0000\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u0000t?9z�\u0000\u0000\u0000(\u0001\u0000\u0000\u001e\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�q\u0000\u0000customXml/_rels/item1.xml.relsPK\u0005\u0006\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0012\u0000\u0012\u0000�\u0004\u0000\u0000�s\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000","minutes_text":"LA VERNE YOUTH & FAMILY ACTION COMMITTEE\n  Minutes of the Regular Meeting\n  June 25, 2024\n\n1. A meeting of the Youth & Family Action Committee was called to order by Council\n  Member Wendy Lau at 5:03 p.m.\n\n  Executive Board Members present:\n\n  Executive Board\n  Wendy Lau, Council Member\n  Greg Palatto, BUSD\n  Denise Fisher, Resident\n  Don Kendrick, Resident\n\n2. Review of Minutes  Minutes for the March 26, 2024, meeting were approved.\n\n3. SRO Report  Student Resource Officer (SRO) Eduardo Burgos shared\n  that graduation was successful and that summer school\n  was happening at Ramona Middle School. He will be\n  keeping in touch with the district and students throughout\n  the summer.\n\n4. BUSD Report  Mark Rodgers shared that there was a smooth end to the\n  school year and a lot of changes within the district. He\n  announced some new leadership including some new\n  principals for the elementary schools. Rodgers also\n  shared that all families who are eligible for free & reduced\n  lunches are guaranteed daycare throughout the summer\n  where students can receive programming, breakfast,\n  lunch and bus transportation.\n\n5. Teach & Transform Grant  All of the accepted grant awardees have accepted and\n  received their funds for their programs. They expressed\n  their thanks to the committee for supporting their\n  initiatives.\n\n6. Summer Lunch  Assistant City Manager JR Ranells talked about the\n  history of the program including that last year was our\n  biggest year with over 3,000 meals handed out at Los\n  Flores Park throughout the summer. In the 3rd week of\n  the program numbers were jumping to close to 80 meals\n  per day. The committee was unable to receive the Tri-\n  Cities grant (approximately $7,000 for the past few\n  summers), but has fundraised almost $7,600 so far this\n  year. He shared that staff is looking at how they can be\n  more efficient in handing out those meals to make sure\n  we’re supporting the right people. Starting Monday, kids\n\fYouth & Family Action Committee Minutes June 25, 2024, page 2\n\n  will need to be present and we will be limiting our number\n  of meals to 60 due to the number of lunches being\n  provided and budget constraints.\n\n7. Fall Programs  Assistant City Manager JR Ranells shared that a\n  discussion was necessary to look at what programs the\n  committee wants to target and how it would want to fund\n  those projects. There is approximately $10,000 of budget\n  to put towards the art projects from the Ruth Reed\n  Foundation grant. The group discussed various art\n  programs including program ideas that could help support\n  underserved students or encourage career exploration.\n\n8. Finance Updates  There are approximately $5,000 of carryover funds\n  currently in the bank that could be used to help cover the\n  cost of the summer lunch program in addition to any\n  donations raised for the program. The committee\n  approved the motion to allocate those $5,000 towards the\n  lunch program if necessary.\n\n9. Recognition of Mark Rodgers The committee presented a certificate to Mark Rodgers\n  for his dedication to YFAC and the Bonita Unified School\n  District and congratulated him on his upcoming\n  retirement.\n\n10. Cancellation of July Meeting The executive board approved unanimously to cancel the\n  July meeting and set the next meeting for August.\n\n11. Public Comment  La Verne Firefighter Kenny Villasenor shared with the\n  group about the LVFD Explorers Program which is open\n  to 15-20 year olds who are interested in the fire service\n  and volunteering. The Explorer Program has a capacity\n  of 20 volunteers at a time and the goal is that they could\n  begin to set themselves up for a career in the fire service\n  with La Verne or other agencies. Police Community\n  Services Supervisor Hollie Savage reported to the group\n  that there will be an additional crossing guard this year\n  who will be stationed at Grace Miller. She also shared\n  with the committee that National Night Out will be taking\n  place on August 6 at Las Flores Park.\n\n7. Next Meeting  The next YFAC meeting was scheduled for August 27,\n  2024 at 5:00pm.\n\n8. Adjournment  The meeting was adjourned at 6:03 p.m.\n\fYouth & Family Action Committee Minutes June 25, 2024, page 3\n\nRespectfully submitted,\n\nErin Beilstein\nSenior Management Analyst","tries":1}